  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Riflesso Menu Milan 00:00 Overview Buy Riflesso [email protected] Instagram Via Tortona, Milan Work Artists Films Archive Journal About Contact One week on the coast road Carmen on shooting Coast Road with a rented car, no plan and a list of towns. Published 15 September 2026 Reading time 2 min All journal posts Coast Road started as a holiday. Carmen rented a small car in Genoa, packed one camera and two lenses, and gave herself a town a day along the Ligurian coast. There was no client and no deadline, only a list of names on the back of a ferry ticket. She had been shooting still life in the studio for most of the year, and she wanted to work outside again, with whatever the street gave her. The rule Only cars that were already parked. No moving anything, no asking owners to wait, no coming back the next day for better light. If the colour was right and the car was there, she shot it. If not, she walked on. The rule sounds strict, but it made the week easy. There was nothing to plan. Every morning she parked outside town, walked in with the camera and stayed until lunch. Afternoons were for driving, swimming and looking at the frames on a laptop in whatever room ",
